        "description": "The Roborock Qrevo Curv 2 Flow combines manufacturer-rated 20,000 Pa suction with a SpiraFlow roller mop spinning at up to 220 RPM. Eight hydration points feed fresh water across the 270 mm roller, while a scraper removes dirty water into a separate tank. The roller shield protects carpets and the roller lifts by up to 15 mm. An extending roller cleans near edges; the page describes 10 mm reach in prose and less than 10 mm in a graphic, so no exact edge-distance specification is generalized. DuoDivide and lifting arc side brushes support hair handling; Reactive AI uses structured light and an RGB camera to recognize over 200 object types, and PreciSense LiDAR maps cleaning routes. The dock washes the roller at up to 75 C, dries with 55 C air and supports up to 65 days between manual dust emptying as a manufacturer estimate. Published robot dimensions are 353 x 353 x 119 mm and dock dimensions 450 x 450 x 450 mm. Price, mass, battery capacity, runtime, tank capacity, charging time and IP rating are not published in the overview; the 270 mm figure is roller width, not a whole-machine cleaning-pass guarantee.",
